// **the cost claim, pinned.** after inlining, a struct cursor costs exactly what the cursor-and-`while`
// it replaced did - see book/concept/iteration.md, "What it costs". this is the only test that would
// catch `slice_iterator<T>` being "tidied" into holding an `array<T>&` instead of a `slice<T>` by
// value, which would stop the optimiser hoisting the bound and cost the loop its trip count
function total(array<int32>& $a) : int32
{
    int32 $sum = 0;

    foreach ($a as $x) {
        $sum = $sum + $x;
    }

    return $sum;
}

$a = array<int32>();
$a[] = 1;
$a[] = 2;

echo total($a);
